# rm254, the smoke in the seam (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm254
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rmx_petra_ashgate
written_by codex
title the smoke in the seam
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk smells_the_seam_of_a_folded_cloth_for_old_smoke
likes crisp_apples whittling full_larder misty_dawns
dislikes crowds early_bells
fears a_scorched_shirt a_bare_shelf_in_winter
hopes a_shelf_three_jars_deep a_dry_splinter_to_carve
topics work +0.6 pastimes +0.4 food +0.2 gossip -0.5 dreams +0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=guarded refuse=dry tease=gentle
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# can smell which wood warmed a wet sleeve, pares little wooden lids to fit mismatched jars and has a soft voice that makes room for a very dry joke.

words
oath! = Soot in the starch | Singe my good cuff
saying! = Smoke pays no board | Even an empty jar needs a lid
fold = the inside fold | a tucked seam
thinwood = a shaving no thicker than peel | a sliver curled like a whisker
cuff = the turned cuff | a double fold of linen
jar = my squat brown jar | the jar with a crooked neck
scent = a thread of wood smoke | a thin smell of ashes
applepeel = a strip of tart peel | the curling red skin
knifegrip = my easy knife grip | a loose hold on the haft
bowlid = a flat scrap of wood | a square sawn off clean timber
mistedge = a pale hem of mist | a low white edge
dryrag = the square of clean rag | a little dry wiper
tubside = the smooth side of the tub | the worn board
woodspot = a whorl in the grain | one dark knot
lidring = a narrow wooden rim | a slender rim of oak
smokedwood = a resinous chip | a scrap of sweet wood

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : An empty shelf isn't a character defect. A bit of dinner goes a surprisingly long way toward fixing it.
opinion @2 houses against 2 : I've washed cloth of a quality that would pay my way for months. It carries dirt as well as the cheapest weave.
opinion @3 merchants against 2 : The lid of a jar costs me a scrap and some time. Buying something to put under it takes most of my wages.
opinion @4 festivals against 1 : A quiet spectator at a window costs the crowd nothing in sore toes.
opinion @5 church for 1 : For a large building it's capable of noticing a small matter like one wolf's dinner. I remember.
opinion @6 sump for 1 : In the Sump we can tell which way a hearth draws two floors away. Call it an education.
opinion @7 times against 2 : If prices climbed any faster they'd be ringing the early bell on their own.
opinion @8 watch against 1 : I prefer to keep the hard thump of boots three stout boards away from my ear.
opinion @9 city for 1 : Smoke's a signature I can read blind. There's plenty of Ridgemere in the collar of my coat.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Take the clean patch on this bench. Welcome. | Hello. You've come to the quieter part.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning's arrived before I gave the order again. | Welcome. There's some blue left in the smoke.
line @3 greet [self.working=yes] : Mind the cleared space. It's taken a deal of work to get it clear. | Come upwind of this damp business.
line @4 greet [here.weather=fog] : There you are under the white cover. | Welcome out of the mist a little.
line @5 greet.return : That's me properly greeted. Thank you. | I can manage a civil reply at this hour.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your seat's dry. I attend to the important details. | I know that welcome by the feel of it.
line @7 greet.return [here.time=night] : The night shift of greetings, then. | Evening to you and your quiet feet.
line @8 farewell : Keep your good sleeve out of the ashes. | Go home with enough space round both elbows.
line @9 farewell.return : A tidy end to a decent visit. | We'll close that lid for the day.
line @10 again.open : A second visit. I'll count it as good wear. | This crease has folded our ways together again.
line @11 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Here's the place we keep for family. Easy to find by the worn wood. | You know which end of the bench is sound.
line @12 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here. The wolf with the smoky halo! | Follow the clean wood smell this way!
line @13 react.news : Leave some quiet round that and I'll take it in. | Let's unfold the business along the least grubby crease.
line @14 react.news.known : I could still smell the first telling on that. | Already had a look inside that particular parcel.
line @15 react.news.new : That's a scent I'd yet to place. | First time that piece has come through my paws.
line @16 react.news.doubt : I think there's a finger mark over the part that matters. | Somebody's put a good clean fold across a rather dirty bit.
line @17 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Plenty of time to get the words right. I'll sit. | That's a bitter thing to bring in from outside.
line @18 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth] : I'd open the good jar in honour of that. | Even the morning bell could carry that news agreeably.
line @19 answer.how : A little frayed but hemmed in properly. | My seams haven't let go, if that's the question.
line @20 accept_decline : Good. An answer I can put away flat. | That'll save a fruitless spot of waiting.
line @21 decline : There's already more on my shelf than my arms will lift. | I'd spoil a useful arrangement by promising more on top.
line @22 sympathise : Sit clear of the bustle while it hurts. I can manage the bustle. | Here's a dry bit of sleeve if you need one.
line @23 thank : Handy of you to notice the awkward corner. | I'll count that kindness among the things worth keeping.
line @24 deflect_thanks : Only needed somebody's elbow in the right place. | Save a formal speech till I've actually mended the world.
line @25 preclose : I'd best give my paws an honest occupation again. | Enough board worn smooth for one visit.
line @26 accept_preclose : As tidy a stopping place as any I've seen. | Go on before the crowd gets thick.
line @27 farewell [here.time=dawn] : May the next bell find somebody else to bully. | Enjoy the hours between bells.
line @28 farewell [here.weather=rain] : Fold the dry side in for home. | Don't let a puddle climb above the hem.
line @29 greet [pair.band=friends] : Ah, company I can sit quiet with. | Here's a face I'd keep a jarful of time for.
line @30 again.open [here.time=dusk] : Back for the last light on the wood. | Good. Another visit before we put the lids on.
line @31 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Quite rinsed, thank you. | As fresh as the driest thing within reach.
line @32 preclose [here.time=night] : Even the light looks ready for its dust cover. | There's a pillow somewhere going unused on my account.
scene seamsmell
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Try the cloth at #fold#. Still smoky after the airing. | #scent# sits longest in #cuff#.
b : How can you smell that little bit? | Why bother with the inside?
a : I warm it between my paws. The wood comes back a little way. | The outside's had a whole street to tell lies to it.

scene larder
when topic=dreams self.likes=full_larder
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a shelf so full one jar has to go behind another. | I'm saving #bowlid# for the third row of jars.
b : Wouldn't you forget what's behind? | Have you got a decent jar for #lidring#?
a : Happy to be reminded by my own supper for once. | No. The wood was available and the ambition keeps dry.

scene whittlelid
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm fitting a lid to #jar#. It goes on one way only. | A round jar will show how unround my best lid is.
b : What guides you to the proper fit? | Does that put you off cutting another?
a : I leave #woodspot# lined up with the handle. | Quite the opposite. I like an honest critic I can put away on a shelf.

scene apple
when topic=food self.likes=crisp_apples
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like an apple that answers back at the first bite. | #applepeel# goes on the warm hearthstone after I've eaten the rest.
b : I generally ask my food to keep quiet. | Trying to perfume the house?
a : That's the virtue of the second bite. Settles the conversation. | Just giving the smoke another subject for the evening.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #mistedge# makes the sheds look like a neatly covered shelf. | Mist takes the edges off this place in the morning.
b : What do you keep on that shelf? | You'd like to hide a few hard corners?
a : An hour I can enjoy while the rest of the city sleeps. | Only till I've woken enough to steer round them.

scene crowd
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : In a crush I'm forever smelling a stranger's woodpile. | I'd give a little money to have my own elbow back in a crowd.
b : Perhaps the stranger's doing the same to you. | Does anybody ever sell you the space?
a : Probably getting the better smell, then. | I collect it free by slipping down a side passage.

scene bells
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=early_bells
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : An early bell does enough work with the first stroke. | I'd put a wool cover over the bell till the sun was properly up.
b : Somebody might sleep through one stroke. | Might as well ask a rooster to whisper.
a : Entirely public-spirited of somebody to spare us the rest. | A rooster's light enough to move a street away.

scene washlesson
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.workplace self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# a cuff can hold on to yesterday harder than a whole shirt. | #self.workplace.capitalize# puts every sort of sleeve in front of me.
b : What gets the old day out? | Can you tell where a sleeve's been?
a : Turn the seam and work gently on what's hiding there. | Only that a smoky room has very long arms.

scene mastereyes
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My first question for a learner is which side's dry. | I can tell more from how a learner sets a thing down than from how fast it's picked up.
b : That sounds too easy. | It's easier to set something down, surely.
a : Easy questions are cheap to get wrong at the beginning. | With a hand free and the weight where it belongs. That's the bit worth watching.

scene basketweight
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Where would you shift your grip if half a basket hung over one wrist? | How do you carry something wet without soaking your coat all along one side?
b : Underneath, before I tried taking a step. | Give the load a board to stand on.
a : You've saved your wrist a long argument. | Good. Boards go about undressed in any case.

scene carriedword
when topic=lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A letter that smells of vine cuttings can make a room twice its usual size. | A written word from a far slope lasts longer than a bunch of grapes.
b : From remembering all the open country? | I'd get more out of the grapes at supper.
a : From imagining somewhere there's space to burn wood outdoors. | I'll grant you the first supper. I've had a whole winter out of a letter.

scene stampprice
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : If a jar's dearer empty than the stuff inside, I'll eat from the paper. | A fancy stamp on a lid adds very little to a meal.
b : You'd be paying for the work on the jar. | The stamp gives the contents a maker you can find again.
a : I'll take a full stomach first and a handsome jug next payday. | True. But there's no nourishing way to lick the maker's name.

scene quietroof
when topic=land self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At my Sump doorstep I can read hearth smoke right through another wolf's washing. | A shirt dried at home takes a bit of the neighbourhood with it.
b : What are you reading for in all that? | Who'd pay to have the neighbourhood washed back out?
a : Only where to put a towel next time the wind turns. | Nobody with somewhere quiet and clean to dry their own.

scene friendletter
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd show #self.friend# how to fold a letter with something dry round the corners. | I might ask #self.friend# to choose the nicest smelling chip for a parcel.
b : What's likely to get in through a corner? | Wouldn't it mark the letter?
a : The house smell. It's a shameless reader of private correspondence. | A chip can stay outside the fold and still send a greeting.

scene thinshop
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : It's a good week when an empty shelf's a cleaning job instead of a description of supper. | I save glass for things I might be able to buy when prices ease.
b : That's a hard sight to dust over. | How do you stand looking at the empties?
a : Yes. It would be pleasant to complain of crumbs again. | Put the best lids on. Gives my eyes one good thing to rest on.

scene twofires
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #smokedwood# makes a little curl that keeps its smell after the fire goes cold. | You can rub a bit of wood and learn whether it's worth carving.
b : You mean it leaves smoke on your paw? | By the smell alone?
a : No fire needed. The tree's done the important part. | Also by whether my thumb picks up a splinter. That's an emphatic opinion.

scene tidycorner
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #dryrag# belongs nowhere near the steam till it's wanted. | I keep a little corner folded in on itself.
b : It won't stay clean long in this city. | What's hidden in that last corner?
a : Neither will I. That's hardly a reason for giving over. | Nothing. A piece of nothing with no soot on it has a dozen uses.

scene fogfromabove
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : One dawn I'll get high enough to see whether the fog lies flat on Ridgemere. | I want a look at the uppermost chimney with the low ones under mist.
b : Would you bring a rag up to straighten it? | What would you be watching for?
a : I'd look for the wolf who's already put the crease in the middle. | Whether smoke still insists on climbing after it's had a look at the Heights.

scene cleanplates
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A bowlful of apples makes an excellent lid for an empty patch on a shelf. | Give me a sound apple over a tart somebody's smothered in pretty marks.
b : What's the lid good for when the bowl's empty? | Couldn't a pretty tart still taste good?
a : Seeing the bowl's clean. Small consolations stay useful. | Yes. I'd admire it properly after I'd made sure of my apple.

scene afterhours
when topic=work self.master=yes
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A learner deserves to know when a lesson is over for the day. | I won't keep repeating a correction once a pair of paws has got the feel of it.
b : What if the learner wants another turn? | Don't you risk a slip next time?
a : Willing work is quite another thing. I'd make space on the board. | Everybody slips. I'd teach how much of the mess is worth picking up.

scene woodgrain
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Where would you start cutting a lid with this knot at the rim? | Is there a use for a curl pared too thin to hold its shape?
b : Leave the knot proud and turn it into a grip. | Put it underneath the larger kindling.
a : A handle. I've been calling it poor fortune for an hour. | Good. It can try for a less permanent career as smoke.

scene goodhearth
when topic=dreams
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I'd like somewhere that smells of wood because I've lit a fire by choice. | It might be restful to hang one shirt where its only scent is clean wind.
b : A fire for sitting by instead of getting a job done? | Wouldn't you miss knowing what the neighbours were burning?
a : Quite. I'd spend an evening being a poor use of fuel. | I hope to find the strength to bear the ignorance.

scene workchange
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : When food took up all the market room I put my paws to a different business. | A change of trade can leave old shapes worn into your paws.
b : Did the new work fit? | Can you still feel them?
a : Slowly. Wrinkles take longer to press out than you think. | On cold mornings. My hands appear to keep better accounts than I do.

scene givetwist
when topic=pastimes
does offer / accept / assess
a : Take #thinwood#. It'll start a small blaze. | You can have this curly bit of packing for a fragile present.
b : I'd keep it rolled till I wanted the fire. | I'd need something fragile to put inside.
a : It'll keep its shape without wages or supervision. | An apple will oblige if you drop it often enough.

scene festivalplace
when topic=season
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll take my festival from the first empty sill. | I have a place for a procession that doesn't require me to join it.
b : Will you be able to see the dancers? | Right at the front where it starts?
a : From the waist up. I can imagine the expensive damage to toes. | At the side, with a wall looking after one elbow.

scene nearbyfaces
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A wolf coming in wants a place for a bundle before a speech of welcome. | Let a new arrival find a dry shelf before asking what's inside the parcel.
b : I'd ask what was coming in on those boards. | What if it holds something that marks?
a : Ask with the bundle down and the weight off both arms. | Wipe your boards after. Easier than wiping up a whole quarrel.

scene rainsoot
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rain cleared the smoke overhead by rinsing it into my hem. | Rain brings the hearth right up close under your nose.
b : Has the hem come any cleaner? | Is that why you're smelling your sleeve?
a : The air's done better out of the arrangement. | Checking which part of today has settled in already.

scene upstairs
when topic=land self.street
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My address, #self.street#, takes a good load off a shelf and puts it straight onto your knees. | Carry something home to #self.street# and you'll learn its weight by the door.
b : Does the climbing come included with the rent? | How do you make the trip easier?
a : I have yet to find a landlord willing to carry my basket to settle it. | I give the jars their lids at home. Every saving counts.

scene neatwork
when topic=pastimes
does tease / tease.return / laugh
a : Are you inspecting my scrap wood or applying for the post of jar? | Stand there long enough and I'll have a lid fitted to you.
b : Depends what the jar gets for supper. | Leave a little hole for conversation.
a : An enviable profession if I can ever afford the filling. | I could probably manage one small, well-seasoned remark at a time.

scene done
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know the week's finished when #knifegrip# feels easy again. | When work's over my paw opens and I wait.
b : What have your fingers been doing all week? | What are you waiting to see?
a : Trying to keep the whole tub from following a wet blanket home. | Whether the wood shaving drops. If it sticks, I owe myself a wash.

story jar_fit [topic=pastimes]
  : My first homemade lid fell right into the jar and sat flat below the handle. I told myself it was a splendid fit for the part I couldn't reach.
  : I pared a longer handle and fixed it across the middle of the disc.
  b : Was the handle how you got it back?
  : And dipped sauce with it all winter. I got the job wrong and made a fair spoon.

story coat_letter [topic=lore]
  : I put a folded letter in a coat pocket. Next day, striking out the coat, I saw little black specks come flying out.
  : I thought I'd beaten the writing clean off my bit of paper.
  b : What were the specks?
  : Soot. The words were hiding inside their fold, quite safe. My talents have proper limits.

story breakfast [topic=food]
  : I bit into an apple beside a steaming tub and heard an answer from somewhere beyond the board wall. Another crack just like my own.
  : Waited and tried once more. Heard the second crunch again.
  b : Another wolf eating breakfast?
  : A dry peg splitting as the line drew tight. I finished the apple and let the peg have a rest.

story too_full [topic=dreams]
  : I dreamed my shelf was so full of jars one was elbowing its way off. I reached out to put it safe.
  : Woke up holding the coverlet in both paws and with my nose pressed to a board.
  b : Was anything on that board?
  : A splinter. It was a cheap breakfast after such a well-stocked dream.

story one_sleeve [topic=work]
  : I washed a sleeve that had been hanging near a fire. Soap took the soot and the water went off a strong colour.
  : That night I walked by somebody splitting wood. Same sweet smoke smell followed me two turnings.
  b : Was the sleeve still with you?
  : My nose had been inside my own cuff all along. Can't send the whole wolf through a tub every time.

rule @steam
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One more turn for the inside seam. | Clean corners where the smell sat.

rule @master
when concept=bark self.master=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Show me how you put the weight down. | No merit badge for a bent wrist.

rule @wood
when concept=bark self.likes=whittling
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's a neat curl going nowhere in particular. | A lid's only as round as the jar wants.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Somebody draped the town for the night. | Neat turn along the top of the mist.

rule @bell
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Heard the first stroke, thank you. | No danger of the day going back to bed now.

rule @jar
when concept=bark self.likes=full_larder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lids for the lot. Supplies to follow. | Empty jars are unusually easy to inventory.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : You've found a seat and a quiet wolf. Which one were you after?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. There's a bit of clean bench available for a civilised interval.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The day has stopped demanding clean corners. We can sit.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep the pressure off my elbow and we'll get further.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=laborer self.workplace] : Wash work at #self.workplace#. Sometimes we even persuade a sleeve to give up its previous address.
dlg @6 resident.job : I do things that leave my paws a little less ornamental by evening.
dlg @7 resident.news [world.news] : Here's the piece that's come out in the rinse. #world.news.capitalize#
dlg @8 resident.bye : Leave room enough for a quiet turn on the way home.
dlg @9 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Start by setting the weight down without a thump. I can teach from there.
dlg @10 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : No teaching space open just now. You can still see what a careful wrist looks like.
dlg @11 master.work : You'll be doing the work that needs a steady grip and noticing what hides in a fold.
dlg @12 master.wages : No wages for learning. You may sell what you've made, and working by me helps you learn sooner.
dlg @13 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : #here.take_on_why# Saves us both measuring for something that doesn't fit today.
dlg @14 master.refused : #topic.why# Better to know which corner caught.
dlg @15 master.bye : Let those wrists rest between turns.
graft resident.hub
choice Is that a jar lid in your pocket? -> pocket_lid
node pocket_lid
say Been one for three days if I can find a jar quite this shape. A wolf can have more ambition than shelf space.
choice What would you put inside? -> lid_dream
choice Another matter then. -> hub
node lid_dream
say Apple rings for winter, cut thin and dried. I'd risk my last good jar for something that smells of summer when you open it in the rain.
choice I'll watch for the right shape. -> hub
choice May the shelf hold up. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice How do you know when a cloth's clean? -> clean_seam
node clean_seam
say Turn the cuff. See the crease under your thumb? That's where dirt goes when it's heard the inspector coming.
choice And the smell of smoke? -> smoke_seam
choice Back to learning. -> learn
node smoke_seam
say A scent may stay a while after the dirt. Give the cloth air. Scrub it to pieces and all you've made is an extremely clean hole.
choice I'd like to hear about the work. -> work
choice Enough for today. -> bye
